# The scripts are bash, and a shell script with CRLF line endings dies on Linux and WSL
# with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M". core.autocrlf=true is the default on
# Windows installs of git, so pin the endings here rather than trusting every clone's
# local config. The source check is compared byte for byte with every plugin's copy, so
# its endings must not depend on the clone either.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
